### Specify a project name with -p for ps and logs

Source: https://github.com/docker/compose/blob/v5.6.1/docs/reference/compose.md

Use the -p flag to set the project name, which takes precedence over COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME, the config file's name:, and directory basenames. Project names must contain only lowercase letters, digits, dashes, and underscores, and begin with a lowercase letter or digit.

```console
$ docker compose -p my_project ps -a
NAME                 SERVICE    STATUS     PORTS
my_project_demo_1    demo       running

$ docker compose -p my_project logs
demo_1  | PING localhost (127.0.0.1): 56 data bytes
demo_1  | 64 bytes from 127.0.0.1: seq=0 ttl=64 time=0.095 ms
```

